course: dictionary
lesson: 2619
title: Who comes after? Descendants
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A descendant is a person who comes later in the same family line. Your mum's mum is your grandmother, so you are her descendant. Your grandmother's children, grandchildren and great-grandchildren are all her descendants. Think of a family tree: the descendants grow down from an earlier person.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Babur, a descendant of Timur and of Genghis Khan, founded the Mughal Empire.» The word «of» tells you whose family line Babur comes from. Timur and Genghis Khan came first, and Babur came after them.
explain: The word is not only for people. «Birds are living descendants of dinosaurs» means birds developed from an earlier kind of animal. Something new can also be a descendant of something older, if it grew out of it. Ask yourself: what came first, and what came after it?
explain: Check your idea by swapping in a simpler phrase. In «The Normans, descendants of Vikings in France, conquered England in 1066», you could say the Normans came after the Vikings and grew out of them. The sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A descendant is a person who comes later in the same family line.
fact: Children, grandchildren and great-grandchildren are all descendants of the people who came before them.
fact: «Descendant» can also mean an animal or plant that has developed from an earlier kind, such as birds from dinosaurs.
fact: In a phrase like «descendants of», the word «of» names the earlier person or thing the line comes from.
fact: «Ancestors» are the people who came before, and «descendants» are the people who come after. The two words go together, like «ancestors and descendants».
exercise: «Babur, a descendant of Timur, founded the Mughal Empire.» What is a descendant? | A soldier in an army | A person who lived before everyone else | *A person who comes later in the same family line | A king who ruled a land
exercise: Birds are living descendants of dinosaurs. What does this tell you? | Birds can talk to dinosaurs | Birds and dinosaurs are the same animal today | *Birds developed from an earlier kind of animal | Dinosaurs are descendants of birds
exercise: «The Normans, descendants of Vikings in France, conquered England in 1066.» Which word tells you the Normans came after the Vikings? | England | 1066 | conquered | *descendants
test: Mia's great-grandfather farmed this land long ago. What is Mia to him? | A king | *A descendant | A neighbour who lives far away | A bird
test: A new apple tree grew from an older apple tree. What is the new tree? | A thunderstorm | A castle | *A descendant | A stone
exam: Which sentence uses descendant correctly? | The sun is a descendant of the moon. | *Ali is a descendant of a famous Scottish chief. | Tuesday is a descendant of the bakery. | Rain is a descendant of the running river.
